    "intro": "Selling gutter cleanings to lawn customers is the easy part. Fitting them into a week that is already full of mowing, aeration and leaf cleanups is where most companies stumble. The mow crew gets pulled off its route to do \"a quick gutter job,\" the quick job takes two hours, and four lawns get pushed to tomorrow. This post is about the scheduling side only: who does the gutter work, how long to budget, how to group stops so the ladder truck is not crossing town, and what to do when rain wipes out a day. Get these few decisions right and gutters become a clean add-on instead of a weekly mess.",
