        "content": "There are three ways lawn companies staff gutters, and each one schedules differently.\n\nThe first is a dedicated gutter crew during the fall and spring waves. Two people, one truck with ladders, and a route of nothing but gutter jobs. This is the cleanest option once you have more than a handful of jobs a week, because the mow routes never get touched.\n\nThe second is a lawn crew that switches to gutters on set days. For example, the crew mows Monday through Thursday and runs gutters Friday. This works well in late October, when mowing visits are shorter and some lawns are skipped.\n\nThe third is tacking a gutter job onto a mowing visit at the same property. It sounds efficient, but it only works for small one-story homes, and only if the crew has the ladder and the time. For anything bigger, it ruins the rest of the route.\n\nPick one approach for the season and stick to it. Mixing all three is how jobs get forgotten."
