        "h2": "Gather the facts once",
        "content": "Every gutter estimate rests on a few facts about the house: how many feet of gutter, how many stories, how steep the roof is, whether there are guards, how many downspouts, and how bad the debris looks. Get them right the first time and you will never have to measure that house again.\n\nFootage can come from a walk around the house with a measuring wheel along the drip line, or from counting the runs and estimating each one. Either is accurate enough for pricing a cleaning. Note which runs are second story; a house with a one-story front and a two-story back is common, and it prices differently from a full two-story.\n\nWrite all of it into the property notes, along with access details like a locked gate or a deck under the back gutter. The next estimate, next season, takes a minute instead of a site visit. Custom fields work well for the numbers you use every time, like footage and story count."
